schema_version: 1
---
title: Message trees, variants, and replies that outlive the browser tab
---
date: 2026-10-18
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: Parity milestones three and four turn messages into a branching tree and run generation as a detached job that clients can leave and rejoin.
---
tags: architecture, sqlite, interface
---
source_commit: 77d71a3f7a923913446048cdc6d991557b1468ea
---
body:

**Message tree.** Messages became a real tree with a remembered selected child,
so editing a message inserts a sibling variant instead of rewriting history,
rerolling creates a new sibling, and forking copies the path from the root. Each
tree edit must present the revision the caller last saw, so a stale browser tab
can never silently overwrite newer work. Threads gained folders, pins, tags,
manual ordering, and content search. Destructively replacing message text was
ruled out, and storing the active path as a list was rejected in favor of a leaf
pointer that survives deletions.

**Detached generation.** Generation now runs on a context independent of the HTTP
request. A job keeps the accumulated text rather than an event log, so a client
that connects, or reconnects, receives a snapshot followed by live updates. Slow
subscribers are dropped instead of buffered. Navigating away stops only the
watcher; Stop remains an explicit call. After an unclean exit, replies still
marked streaming are marked interrupted and never resubmitted.

The same milestone added reply length caps that cut at sentence ends, a reasoning
watchdog, and validated text attachments, plus code copy and save tools and a
jump-to-latest control.

[Commit 77d71a3](https://github.com/Labyricorn/Labbonet/commit/77d71a3f7a923913446048cdc6d991557b1468ea)
